[00:04:30] Jonas Weber: If the delays continue into November, we will have to evaluate other vendors before the renewal. I want that on the record.
[00:05:00] Mei Chen: Noted. We'll also offer you an executive sponsor. I'll introduce Olivia Hart, our VP Customer Success, by October 9.
[00:05:30] Katrin Vogel: Fine. Send everything in writing.$$),
($$meetings-2026-10-01-leadership-offsite$$, $$Leadership Offsite Notes - Q4 2026$$, $$meetings$$, $$Jordan Lee (CEO)$$, $$2026-10-01$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$meetings/2026-10-01-leadership-offsite.md$$, $$# Leadership Offsite - October 1, 2026

## Q4 company goals

1. Reach $48M ARR by December 31 (currently $43.5M).
2. Launch AI Insights beta to 25 customers on November 12.
3. Reduce SEV-1 incidents to zero for the quarter.
4. Hire 18 people, focused on Data Infra and Customer Success.

## Headcount and hiring

- Hiring freeze lifted for Engineering and Customer Success only. All other teams remain at current headcount until Q1 planning.
- Referral bonus raised to $5,000 for engineering roles (was $3,000), effective October 15.

## Office and remote

- The Austin office lease is renewed through 2028.
- No change to the remote work policy; the 2-days-in-office guideline for hub employees remains.

## Budget

- Travel budget for Q4 is cut by 15% versus Q3. Prioritize customer-facing travel. Internal team offsites should be virtual unless approved by a VP.
- The 2026 travel & expense policy (new per diem rates) took effect July 1.$$),
