($$people-oncall-compensation-policy$$, $$On-call Compensation & Recovery Policy$$, $$people$$, $$People Team$$, $$2026-02-01$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$people/oncall-compensation-policy.md$$, $$# On-call Compensation & Recovery Policy

## Stipend

- Primary on-call: $500 per week. Secondary: $250 per week (Lisbon: EUR 300 / EUR 150).

## Recovery time

- Paged between midnight and 6:00 local time: one comp day, to be taken within 30 days.
- Worked a weekend day for an incident or release: one comp day per weekend day.
- Managers must schedule comp days within two weeks; they do not expire while an incident is ongoing.

## Load limits

- No one should be primary on-call more than one week in four. If a rotation falls below 6 people, the manager must add a shared rotation with SRE.$$),
($$people-retention-playbook$$, $$Retention Playbook for Managers and HRBPs$$, $$people$$, $$People Team$$, $$2026-05-12$$, $$managers$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$people/retention-playbook.md$$, $$# Retention Playbook

## Signals worth a conversation (team level first)

- After-hours work or pages well above the team's normal for 3+ weeks.
- PTO not being taken (less than 1 day per person per month).
- A drop in the workload or intent-to-stay scores in the pulse survey.
- Promises made to employees (promotion cases, comp reviews, comp days, staffing) that are overdue.
- Recent voluntary exits in the same team.

## Actions that work

- Keep the promises you made, or re-commit with a new date in writing.
- Reduce load first: shared rotations, backfills, contractors, pausing non-critical work.
- Recovery time: schedule comp days and PTO.
- Career: promotion cases on time; stay interviews with key people.
- Pay: off-cycle reviews need VP and Total Rewards approval (see Compensation Bands).

## Guardrails

- Never use these signals for performance or disciplinary decisions.
- Survey data is anonymous and only shown for groups of 5 or more.
- No individual "flight risk" scores. Talk to people, don't profile them.$$),
($$policies-compensation-bands$$, $$Engineering Compensation Bands 2026$$, $$policies$$, $$People Team (Total Rewards)$$, $$2026-04-01$$, $$managers$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/compensation-bands.md$$, $$# Engineering Compensation Bands 2026 (Managers only)

Confidential. Do not share with individual contributors.

## Base salary bands (US, Tier 1 cities)

| Level | Title | Band |
|---|---|---|
| E3 | Software Engineer | $135,000 - $165,000 |
| E4 | Senior Software Engineer | $170,000 - $210,000 |
| E5 | Staff Engineer | $215,000 - $260,000 |
| E6 | Principal Engineer | $265,000 - $320,000 |

## Adjustments

- Tier 2 US locations: 90% of Tier 1 band. Lisbon hub: 60% of Tier 1 band (paid in EUR).
- Merit cycle happens each March. Off-cycle raises need VP and People Team approval.
- Equity refresh grants are reviewed annually in the merit cycle.$$),
($$policies-pto-policy$$, $$Time Off (PTO) Policy$$, $$policies$$, $$People Team$$, $$2026-01-05$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/pto-policy.md$$, $$# Time Off Policy

## Vacation

- Acme has flexible PTO with a **minimum** of 15 days per year that everyone is expected to take.
- Request time off in the HR Portal at least 2 weeks in advance for absences of 3 days or more.
- On-call engineers must arrange a swap before taking PTO during their rotation.

## Company holidays (US, 2026)

New Year's Day, MLK Day, Presidents Day, Memorial Day, Juneteenth, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving (Thursday and Friday), Christmas Eve, Christmas Day. Plus a company-wide **Recharge Week** from December 28 to December 31.

## Sick leave

- Unlimited sick days for short illnesses; no doctor's note needed for under 5 consecutive days.

## Parental leave

- 16 weeks fully paid for all parents, usable within 12 months of birth or adoption.

## Volunteer time

- 2 paid volunteer days per year.$$),
($$policies-remote-work-policy$$, $$Remote Work Policy$$, $$policies$$, $$People Team$$, $$2026-03-10$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/remote-work-policy.md$$, $$# Remote Work Policy

## Who it applies to

All full-time employees. Acme is remote-friendly with hubs in Austin, New York, and Lisbon.

## Hub employees

- Employees living within 50 miles of a hub are **hub employees** and are expected in the office 2 days per week (Tuesday and Thursday are anchor days).
- Exceptions require manager and People Team approval.

## Fully remote employees

- Employees outside hub radius work fully remote.
- Company covers coworking space up to $250/month if requested.
- Expect to travel to a hub up to 2 times per year for team gatherings (paid by the company).

## Working from another country

- You may work from another country for up to 30 days per calendar year. Submit a request in the HR Portal at least 2 weeks ahead so Legal can check tax and immigration requirements.
- Working from sanctioned countries is not allowed.

## Core hours

Everyone should be available 10:00-14:00 in their team's primary time zone.$$),
($$policies-security-policy$$, $$Information Security Policy$$, $$policies$$, $$Security Team (CISO Hannah Cho)$$, $$2026-05-20$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/security-policy.md$$, $$# Information Security Policy

## Passwords and authentication

- All company systems use SSO with a hardware security key (YubiKey) as the second factor. SMS codes are not permitted.
- Lost a security key? Report it in #security-help immediately; IT ships a replacement the next business day. Use your backup key in the meantime.

## Data classification

- **Public**: marketing site, public docs.
- **Internal**: wiki, meeting notes, roadmaps. Do not share outside Acme.
- **Confidential**: customer data, financials, HR records. Access is need-to-know and logged.
- Customer data must never be copied to personal devices or pasted into unapproved AI tools. The approved AI tools list is maintained in the Internal Tools directory.

## Devices

- Laptops must have disk encryption, auto-lock after 5 minutes, and the endpoint agent installed.
- Personal phones may access Slack and email only after enrolling in device management.

## Reporting a security incident

- Suspected phishing: use the **Report Phish** button in email, or forward to phish@acme.example.
- Any suspected data exposure: page the Security on-call via the Incident Tracker immediately, severity SEV-1 by default.

## Vendor access

- New vendors handling Confidential data require a security review (allow 2-3 weeks). Request via the Vendor Review form.$$),
($$policies-travel-expense-policy-2024$$, $$Travel & Expense Policy (2024)$$, $$policies$$, $$Finance$$, $$2024-02-01$$, $$all$$, $$superseded$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/travel-expense-policy-2024.md$$, $$# Travel & Expense Policy (2024)

## Meals

- Daily meal per diem: **$75** per day for domestic travel, $100 for international.
- Alcohol is not reimbursable.

## Flights

- Economy class for all flights. Premium economy allowed for flights over 8 hours.
- Book at least 14 days in advance when possible.

## Hotels

- Up to $250 per night in major cities, $175 elsewhere.

## Submitting expenses

- Submit within 60 days of the expense with itemized receipts for anything over $25.
- Manager approval required for all expenses.$$),
($$policies-travel-expense-policy-2026$$, $$Travel & Expense Policy (2026)$$, $$policies$$, $$Finance (Rachel Gomez, Controller)$$, $$2026-06-15$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$policies/travel-expense-policy-2026.md$$, $$# Travel & Expense Policy (2026)

Effective **July 1, 2026**. Supersedes the 2024 Travel & Expense Policy.

## Meals

- Daily meal per diem: **$90** per day for domestic travel, **$120** for international.
- Client dinners: up to $150 per person with a VP-approved business purpose. Alcohol is reimbursable only at client dinners, up to 2 drinks per person.

## Flights

- Economy class for flights under 6 hours. Premium economy allowed for flights of 6 hours or more. Business class requires CFO approval.
- Book at least 21 days in advance when possible. Use the travel tool (Navan) for all bookings.

## Hotels

- Up to $300 per night in tier-1 cities (New York, San Francisco, London, Tokyo), $200 elsewhere.

## Ground transport

- Rideshare and taxis are reimbursable. Personal car mileage at the IRS rate.

## Submitting expenses

- Submit within **30 days** of the expense (reduced from 60). Itemized receipts required for anything over $25.
- Expenses under $75 are auto-approved; over $75 require manager approval.
- Late submissions over 90 days are not reimbursed.

## Q4 2026 note

Internal team offsites should be virtual during Q4 2026 unless approved by a VP (per leadership offsite decision).$$),
($$product-ai-token-plans$$, $$AI Token Plans & Overage Policy$$, $$product$$, $$Revenue Operations$$, $$2026-08-20$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/ai-token-plans.md$$, $$# AI Token Plans & Overage Policy (effective September 1, 2026)

Pulse AI features (natural-language query, AI summaries, and AI Insights early access) are metered in tokens (input + output) per workspace per calendar month.

## Plans

| AI plan | Tokens / month | Price | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| AI Starter | 5 million | Included with Enterprise; $49/month on Growth | |
| AI Pro | 25 million | $1,500/month | |
| AI Scale | 100 million | $5,000/month | Volume discounts above 3 workspaces |
| AI Beta (unlimited) | Unlimited | $1,500/month flat | Grandfathered for design partners only, until December 31, 2026. Must move to a metered plan at renewal. |

## Overage

- Usage above the allowance is billed at **$80 per extra million tokens** on the next invoice. There is no hard cap unless the customer opts in.
- **The account's CSM must notify the customer at 80% and again at 100% of the monthly allowance**, and offer a plan change before any overage is invoiced.
- Overage above $2,000 in a month needs a CSM call before the invoice is sent (bill-shock rule).
- Upgrades take effect immediately and are prorated; downgrades take effect at the next renewal.

## Shelfware

- Accounts on AI Pro or AI Scale using less than 10% of their allowance for two months in a row should get an adoption plan from their CSM before renewal.$$),
($$product-ai-unit-economics$$, $$AI Unit Economics (internal)$$, $$product$$, $$Finance (Rachel Gomez, Controller)$$, $$2026-09-15$$, $$managers$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/ai-unit-economics.md$$, $$# AI Unit Economics (internal, managers only)

## Inference cost to Acme

- Blended model cost: **$4 per million input tokens, $20 per million output tokens** (frontier model for AI Insights; same rate used for all AI features in reporting).
- Target AI gross margin: **70% or higher** per account. Accounts below 40% are reviewed by Finance monthly; negative-margin accounts need a pricing change at renewal.

## Watch list

- AI Beta (unlimited) design-partner accounts carry the highest margin risk: long-context AI Insights requests are output-heavy.
- AI Starter on Enterprise is included in the subscription, so its cost is a cost of service with no direct AI revenue.$$),
($$product-pricing$$, $$Pulse Pricing & Plans$$, $$product$$, $$Revenue Operations$$, $$2026-09-01$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/pricing.md$$, $$# Pulse Pricing & Plans

| Plan | Price | Included events / month | Overage | Data retention |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Free | $0 | 1 million | Not available (hard cap) | 3 months |
| Growth | $399/month (billed annually) or $479 monthly | 25 million | $12 per extra million | 13 months |
| Enterprise | Custom (typically from $36,000/year) | Custom | Negotiated | 25 months |

## Add-ons

- **AI features** (natural-language query, AI summaries, AI Insights): metered in tokens since September 1, 2026. See *AI Token Plans & Overage Policy*. Not available on Free.
- **Extra data retention**: +12 months for $150/month (Growth).

## Discounts

- Nonprofits and education: 50% off Growth.
- Startups (under 2 years old, under $5M raised): Growth free for the first year via the Startup Program.
- Sales reps may discount Enterprise up to 15% without approval; 15-25% needs the VP Sales; over 25% needs the CFO.

## Feature availability

- SSO (SAML/OIDC): Growth and Enterprise
- SCIM: Enterprise only
- 99.9% uptime SLA: Enterprise only
- Warehouse sync: Enterprise only$$),
($$product-pulse-overview$$, $$Acme Pulse Product Overview$$, $$product$$, $$Product Marketing$$, $$2026-08-20$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/pulse-overview.md$$, $$# Acme Pulse Product Overview

Acme Pulse is a product analytics platform. Teams use it to track user behavior, build dashboards, and run funnel, retention, and cohort analyses.

## Core features

- **Event tracking** with SDKs for JavaScript, iOS, Android, Python, Go, and a REST API.
- **Dashboards v2**: drag-and-drop dashboards with real-time tiles (replaces Reports v1).
- **Funnels and retention**: conversion funnels with up to 20 steps; retention curves by cohort.
- **Experiments**: A/B test analysis with sequential testing.
- **Alerts**: anomaly alerts delivered to Slack, email, or PagerDuty.
- **Warehouse sync** (Enterprise): nightly sync to Snowflake or BigQuery.

## Coming soon

- **AI Insights** (beta Nov 12, 2026): natural-language questions over your analytics, automatic anomaly explanations.

## Ideal customers

B2B and B2C SaaS companies with 20-2,000 employees. Main competitors: Amplitude, Mixpanel, PostHog.

## Key differentiators

- Unlimited dashboard seats on every plan.
- EU data residency.
- Query engine returns 95% of queries in under 2 seconds.$$),
($$product-release-notes-4-2$$, $$Release Notes - Pulse 4.2$$, $$product$$, $$Product Eng$$, $$2026-09-29$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/release-notes-4.2.md$$, $$# Pulse 4.2 Release Notes (September 29, 2026)

## New

- Funnel step limit raised from 10 to 20 steps.
- Alerts can now post to PagerDuty.
- Dashboard tiles support custom date comparisons ("vs. same period last year").

## Improved

- CSV export is 3x faster for exports under 1 GB.
- iOS SDK reduces battery usage during background sync.

## Fixed

- Retention chart showed wrong cohort sizes when a timezone other than UTC was set.
- SSO login loop for Entra ID users with more than 150 groups.

## Known issues

- Android 15 devices: app may crash when opening a dashboard with more than 12 tiles. Fix coming in 4.3. Workaround: use the web app or split the dashboard.$$),
($$product-roadmap-q4-2026$$, $$Product Roadmap Q4 2026$$, $$product$$, $$Dana Ruiz (VP Product)$$, $$2026-09-30$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/roadmap-q4-2026.md$$, $$# Product Roadmap - Q4 2026

## October

- Release 4.3 (Oct 27): Android 15 crash fix, faster dashboard loading (target -30% load time), new chart types (sankey, heatmap).
- Reports v1 deprecation notice sent to customers on October 15.

## November

- **AI Insights beta** (Nov 12) for 25 selected Growth and Enterprise accounts.
- SCIM provisioning for Okta and Entra ID GA.

## December

- Release 4.4 (Dec 8): session replay alpha, custom roles for Enterprise.
- Code freeze begins December 18.

## Not in Q4 (moved to 2027)

- Self-hosted / on-prem deployment option.
- Native HubSpot integration (moved to Q1 2027).$$),
($$product-sales-battlecard$$, $$Sales Battlecard - Pulse vs Competitors$$, $$product$$, $$Revenue Operations (Kim Alvarez)$$, $$2026-09-18$$, $$sales, managers$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$product/sales-battlecard.md$$, $$# Sales Battlecard: Pulse vs Competitors

Internal only. For Sales and Customer Success.

## vs Amplitude

- Win on: unlimited dashboard seats, EU data residency, price (Growth is ~35% cheaper at 25M events).
- Lose on: depth of behavioral cohort tooling. Don't claim parity on predictive cohorts.

## vs Mixpanel

- Win on: query speed (95% under 2s), warehouse sync on Enterprise.
- Lose on: brand awareness in early-stage startups. Lead with the Startup Program (Growth free for year one).

## vs PostHog

- Win on: enterprise readiness (SCIM, 99.9% SLA, SOC 2 Type II).
- Lose on: self-hosting. We have no on-prem option until 2027; do not promise a date.

## Objection handling

- "AI features?" -> AI Insights beta Nov 12, 2026; Enterprise includes it, Growth is +$49/month.
- "Too expensive?" -> Offer annual billing ($399 vs $479 monthly) before discounting.$$),
($$support-known-issues$$, $$Support Known Issues & Macros$$, $$support$$, $$Support Team (Lead: Ben Torres)$$, $$2026-10-06$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$support/known-issues.md$$, $$# Support Known Issues & Macros

## Known issues

### Android 15 dashboard crash
- Symptom: Pulse Android app crashes on dashboards with more than 12 tiles.
- Status: Fix in release 4.3 (Oct 27).
- Workaround: Use web app, or split dashboard into smaller ones.

### Incorrect invoice after INC-2291
- Symptom: Customer reports an invoice amount was wrong in September 2026 (EUR/GBP customers).
- Status: Resolved. Invoices were voided and reissued.
- Macro: Apologize, confirm the reissued invoice number, and apply a one-month 10% credit (Support leads can apply this in the Billing Admin tool).

### Events delayed in eu-central
- Symptom: Events show up 10-20 minutes late for eu-central workspaces during peak hours.
- Status: Investigating (Data Infra, JIRA DI-4410).
- Response: Data is not lost; it will appear once ingestion catches up.

## Escalation paths

- Billing issues: #team-payments, or escalate in the Support Desk to tier "Billing L2".
- Suspected security issue reported by customer: page Security on-call immediately.
- Enterprise customers with SLA impact: notify their Customer Success Manager within 1 hour.

## Response time targets

- Enterprise: first response within 1 hour (24/7 for SEV-1).
- Growth: first response within 8 business hours.
- Free: community forum only.$$),
($$support-tickets$$, $$Tickets$$, $$support$$, NULL, NULL, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$support/tickets.json$$, $$[
