($$docs-architecture-overview--0$$, $$docs-architecture-overview$$, 0, $$Pulse Architecture Overview$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-07-30$$, NULL, $$Pulse Architecture Overview

# Pulse Architecture Overview$$),
($$docs-architecture-overview--1$$, $$docs-architecture-overview$$, 1, $$Pulse Architecture Overview$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-07-30$$, NULL, $$Pulse Architecture Overview - High-level components

- **Web app**: Next.js frontend served from the edge.
- **API gateway**: Handles auth (SSO/OIDC), rate limiting (600 requests/minute per workspace by default), and routing.
- **Ingest service**: Receives events from customer SDKs, validates them, and writes to Kafka. Handles about 2.1 billion events per day.
- **Query engine**: Runs analytics queries over ClickHouse. Hot data (last 90 days) lives on SSD; older data is in object storage.
- **Billing service**: Computes usage from event counts, syncs invoices to Stripe nightly at 02:00 UTC.
- **Postgres**: Stores workspaces, users, dashboards, and permissions.$$),
($$docs-architecture-overview--2$$, $$docs-architecture-overview$$, 2, $$Pulse Architecture Overview$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-07-30$$, NULL, $$Pulse Architecture Overview - Data retention

- Raw events: 13 months on Growth plan, 25 months on Enterprise.
- Aggregated metrics: retained indefinitely.
- Deleted workspaces are purged after 30 days.$$),
($$docs-architecture-overview--3$$, $$docs-architecture-overview$$, 3, $$Pulse Architecture Overview$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-07-30$$, NULL, $$Pulse Architecture Overview - Regions

Pulse runs in two regions: `us-east` (default) and `eu-central`. EU customers can pin data residency to `eu-central`; data never leaves the region.$$),
($$docs-architecture-overview--4$$, $$docs-architecture-overview$$, 4, $$Pulse Architecture Overview$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-07-30$$, NULL, $$Pulse Architecture Overview - Service ownership

| Service | Team | Slack |
|---|---|---|
| API gateway | Platform | #team-platform |
| Ingest | Data Infra | #team-data-infra |
| Query engine | Data Infra | #team-data-infra |
| Billing | Payments | #team-payments |
| Web app | Product Eng | #team-product-eng |$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--0$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 0, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook

# Deploy Runbook$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--1$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 1, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook - Deploy windows

- Production deploys are allowed Monday to Thursday, 9:00-16:00 Pacific.
- **No deploys on Fridays** or the day before a company holiday, except for hotfixes approved by the on-call Incident Commander.
- Deploy freeze for the year-end period runs from December 18 to January 4.$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--2$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 2, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook - Standard deploy steps

1. Merge your PR to `main`. CI builds a release artifact automatically.
2. In the Deploy Console (go/deploy), select the build and click **Deploy to staging**.
3. Run the smoke test suite: `make smoke ENV=staging`. All checks must pass.
4. Promote to production with **Canary 10%**. Watch the Pulse Health dashboard for 15 minutes.
5. If error rate stays under 0.5% and p95 latency stays under 400ms, promote to 100%.
6. Post a message in #deploys with the build number and a summary.$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--3$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 3, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook - Rollback

- In the Deploy Console, click **Rollback** on the previous healthy build. Rollback takes about 3 minutes.
- Database migrations must be backwards-compatible for one release so rollback is always safe.
- After a rollback, open an incident in the Incident Tracker if customers were affected.$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--4$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 4, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook - Feature flags

- All user-facing changes ship behind a feature flag in FlagHouse.
- Flags must be removed within 30 days of reaching 100% rollout.$$),
($$docs-deploy-runbook--5$$, $$docs-deploy-runbook$$, 5, $$Deploy Runbook$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-25$$, NULL, $$Deploy Runbook - Changes since the September incident

After the 2026-09-19 billing outage (see the incident review), canary duration was raised from 5 minutes to 15 minutes, and any deploy that touches the `billing` service now requires a second approver from the Payments team.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--0$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 0, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide

# Engineering Onboarding Guide

Welcome to Acme engineering! This guide covers your first two weeks.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--1$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 1, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide - Day 1: Accounts and access

- Your laptop is pre-provisioned by IT. Sign in with your Acme SSO account.
- Request GitHub access through the **Access Portal** (go/access). Select the `acme-eng` group. Approval is automatic for engineers.
- Request AWS read-only access via the Access Portal (`aws-readonly`). Production write access (`aws-prod-deploy`) requires manager approval and completion of the Production Safety training.
- Join Slack channels: #eng-general, #eng-help, #deploys, #incidents.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--2$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 2, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide - Day 2-3: Local development environment

1. Install Homebrew, then run `brew bundle` in the `acme/dev-setup` repo.
2. Clone the `pulse` monorepo and run `make bootstrap`. This installs Node 24, pnpm, Postgres 17 via Docker, and seeds a local database.
3. Run `make dev` to start the API on port 4000 and the web app on port 3000.
4. If `make bootstrap` fails on Apple Silicon with a Docker platform error, set `DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM=linux/arm64` and retry.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--3$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 3, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide - Week 1: Your first change

- Every new engineer ships a small change in week one. Your onboarding buddy will pick a `good-first-issue` ticket with you.
- All PRs need one approving review and green CI. Use conventional commit titles (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Read the Deploy Runbook before your first deploy. New engineers deploy with their buddy for their first two deploys.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--4$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 4, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide - Week 2: Production readiness

- Complete Production Safety training (in the LMS, about 45 minutes).
- Shadow one on-call shift. Ask the current on-call engineer in #oncall.
- You join the on-call rotation after 6 weeks.$$),
($$docs-engineering-onboarding--5$$, $$docs-engineering-onboarding$$, 5, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide$$, $$docs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-08-14$$, NULL, $$Engineering Onboarding Guide - Who to ask

- Onboarding questions: your buddy, or #eng-help
- Access problems: #it-help or the IT Service Desk tool
- Engineering Enablement owner: Priya Nair$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--0$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 0, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public)

# Pulse Customer FAQ$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--1$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 1, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - Can I export my data?

Yes. Any admin can export raw events as CSV or Parquet from **Settings > Data > Export**. Exports over 10 GB are delivered to an S3 bucket you configure. Enterprise customers can also use the nightly warehouse sync to Snowflake or BigQuery.$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--2$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 2, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - Do you support SSO?

SAML and OIDC SSO are available on Growth and Enterprise. SCIM user provisioning is Enterprise-only.$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--3$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 3, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - Where is my data stored?

In the `us-east` region by default. Customers can choose `eu-central` at workspace creation for EU data residency. Region cannot be changed after creation without a migration request to Support.$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--4$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 4, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - What happens if I exceed my event quota?

We never drop your data. Overage is billed at the plan's per-million-event rate. You get an email alert at 80% and 100% of quota.$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--5$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 5, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - How do I cancel?

Admins can cancel from **Settings > Billing**. Annual contracts cancel at the end of the term. Monthly plans cancel at the end of the current billing period; no partial refunds.$$),
($$faqs-customer-faq--6$$, $$faqs-customer-faq$$, 6, $$Customer FAQ (Public)$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-15$$, NULL, $$Customer FAQ (Public) - Is there an uptime SLA?

Enterprise plans include a 99.9% monthly uptime SLA with service credits. Growth and Free plans have no contractual SLA.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--0$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 0, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ

# Employee FAQ$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--1$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 1, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - When is payday?

Acme pays semi-monthly, on the 15th and the last business day of each month. If the 15th falls on a weekend, pay is issued the prior Friday.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--2$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 2, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - How do I update my direct deposit or tax withholding?

In the HR Portal (go/hr) under **Pay > Payment Methods**. Changes made before the 5th or the 20th apply to the next paycheck.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--3$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 3, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - What is the learning & development budget?

Each employee has $1,500 per calendar year for courses, books, and conferences. Submit through the expense tool under the category "Learning". Unused budget does not roll over.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--4$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 4, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - How do I get a new monitor or equipment?

File a request in the IT Service Desk. Standard equipment (monitor, keyboard, mouse, headset) ships in 3-5 business days. Home office stipend is a one-time $500 for new hires.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--5$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 5, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - Who do I contact about benefits?

Email benefits@acme.example or post in #ask-people. Open enrollment runs November 3-17, 2026.$$),
($$faqs-employee-faq--6$$, $$faqs-employee-faq$$, 6, $$Employee FAQ$$, $$faqs$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-02$$, NULL, $$Employee FAQ - How does the referral program work?

Submit referrals in the Recruiting tool. If your referral is hired and stays 90 days, you receive the bonus: $5,000 for engineering roles (effective October 15, 2026) and $2,000 for all other roles.$$),
($$meetings-2026-09-08-product-sync--0$$, $$meetings-2026-09-08-product-sync$$, 0, $$Product Sync - 2026-09-08$$, $$meetings$$, $$all$$, $$current$$, NULL, NULL, $$2026-09-08$$, NULL, $$Product Sync - 2026-09-08

